# XCU comm
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Inputs are ordered by byte value, which is the collating sequence of the
# POSIX locale used by the tests.

assertion  XCU.comm.001
anchor     utilities/comm.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/comm.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       comm writes lines found only in file1 as they are, lines found
           only in file2 after one tab, and lines found in both after two
           tabs, in the order of the inputs.
test       t/001-three-columns.sh

assertion  XCU.comm.002
anchor     utilities/comm.html#OPTIONS/-1
anchor     utilities/comm.html#OPTIONS/-2
anchor     utilities/comm.html#OPTIONS/-3
anchor     utilities/comm.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       comm -1, -2 and -3 each leave out one column; the lines of the
           columns after it then have one tab less, except that lines in
           both files get one tab when exactly one of -1 and -2 is given.
test       t/002-suppress-one-column.sh

assertion  XCU.comm.003
anchor     utilities/comm.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       With two of the options the remaining column is written with no
           tab in front, and with all three nothing is written.
test       t/003-suppress-two-columns.sh

assertion  XCU.comm.004
anchor     utilities/comm.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/comm.html#STDIN
class      required
since      1992
says       The operand - as file1 or file2 means standard input.
test       t/004-standard-input.sh

assertion  XCU.comm.005
anchor     utilities/comm.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       When file1 or file2 cannot be read the status is nonzero.
test       t/005-unreadable-file.sh
